cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below."
title: "TIR-A: An 8 GiB-First Local Inference Engine on Windows (llama.cpp fork + 14-function C ABI)"
authors:
  - name: "TIR-A contributors"
date-released: 2026-11-10
url: "https://github.com/Across2005/tir-a-8gb-inference"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Across2005/tir-a-8gb-inference"
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  A staged engineering report on building an in-process local inference DLL for
  a single Windows laptop with an 8 GiB RTX 5060 Laptop GPU, covering a 14-function
  C ABI, MTP speculative decoding, chunked prefill, measurement discipline, and
  the hardware limits that stop 8B models at roughly 57 tok/s.
keywords:
  - local inference
  - llama.cpp
  - C ABI
  - MTP
  - CUDA
  - Windows
  - GGUF
